sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: The square on a minor straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth a fourth apotome.
----
proof:

Let {AB} be a minor and {CD} a rational straight line, and to the rational straight line {CD} let {CE} be applied equal to the square on {AB} and producing {CF} as breadth.

I say that {CF} is a fourth apotome.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="370" height="180" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.100 diagram" src="propX100.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure (X.99's): the minor AB with its annex BG on the line
    // AG, the rational CD, CE (DCFE) equal to the square on AB applied to CD
    // with breadth CF, CH equal to the square on AG (DCFE with FKHE), KL
    // (HKML) equal to the square on BG, FM bisected at N and the parallel NO.
    // Added, all hidden at rest: solid twins AB and BG (initiallyHidden) so
    // AB stands alone and the annex is produced from B to G; transparent
    // targets CF, CK, KH, KM, CM, FM, MN, EF, ML (;0;0;0); faceless
    // rectangles CE, CH, KL, CL, FL, FO, NL (;0;0;0;0) for the areas the
    // text names, since the random-faced originals would be raised over the
    // figure when lit (#140). No angle is called right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D, G (line sliders)
    // and the offscreen frees. C and D arrive with "CD a rational straight
    // line", G with the annex, so all three are deferred. F, E, K, H, M, L,
    // N, O are derived and listed per slide.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","AB"];
    var RAT   = GIVEN.concat(["C","D","CD"]);
    var APPL  = RAT.concat(["F","E","DCFE","CE","CF"]);
    var ANNEX = APPL.concat(["G","BG"]);
    var GA    = ANNEX.concat(["AG"]);
    var CHS   = GA.concat(["K","H","FKHE","CH","CK"]);
    var KLS   = CHS.concat(["M","L","HKML","KL","KM","KH","CL","CM","FL","FM","ML"]);
    var ALL   = KLS.concat(["N","O","NO","FO","NL","MN","EF"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "X.100",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,40;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,40;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;40,-1000;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;40,1000;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,120,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,190,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,70",
            "D;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,0,140",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "F';point;parallelogram;C,A0,A3;0;0",
            "F;point;proportion;C,D,A,B,A,B,C,F'",
            "E;point;parallelogram;D,C,F",
            "DCFE;polygon;quadrilateral;D,C,F,E;0;0;black;random",
            "G;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,250,0",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G",
            "K;point;proportion;C,D,A,G,A,G,C,F'",
            "H;point;parallelogram;D,C,K",
            "FKHE;polygon;quadrilateral;F,K,H,E;0;0;black;random",
            "M;point;proportion;C,D,B,G,B,G,K,F'",
            "L;point;parallelogram;D,C,M",
            "HKML;polygon;quadrilateral;H,K,M,L;0;0;black;random",
            "N;point;midpoint;F,M",
            "O;point;parallelogram;D,C,N",
            "NO;line;connect;N,O",
            // Slide-only twins and highlight targets.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "BG;line;connect;B,G",
            "CF;line;connect;C,F;0;0;0",
            "CK;line;connect;C,K;0;0;0",
            "KH;line;connect;K,H;0;0;0",
            "KM;line;connect;K,M;0;0;0",
            "CM;line;connect;C,M;0;0;0",
            "FM;line;connect;F,M;0;0;0",
            "MN;line;connect;M,N;0;0;0",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F;0;0;0",
            "ML;line;connect;M,L;0;0;0",
            "CE;polygon;quadrilateral;C,F,E,D;0;0;0;0",
            "CH;polygon;quadrilateral;C,K,H,D;0;0;0;0",
            "KL;polygon;quadrilateral;K,M,L,H;0;0;0;0",
            "CL;polygon;quadrilateral;C,M,L,D;0;0;0;0",
            "FL;polygon;quadrilateral;F,M,L,E;0;0;0;0",
            "FO;polygon;quadrilateral;F,N,O,E;0;0;0;0",
            "NL;polygon;quadrilateral;N,M,L,O;0;0;0;0"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["AB","BG"],
        deferDraggables: ["C","D","G"],
        aliases: { "GB": "BG", "LF": "FL", "MF": "FM", "NM": "MN", "FE": "EF" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“The square on a minor straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB", "CD", "CE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.100" }] },
            { text: "produces as breadth a fourth apotome.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Let {AB} be a minor",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB"] },
            { text: "and {CD} a rational straight line,",
              visible: RAT,
              highlighted: ["CD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "C", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "D", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "and to the rational straight line {CD} let {CE} be applied equal to the square on {AB}",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CD", "AB"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "DCFE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and producing {CF} as breadth.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "I say that {CF} is a fourth apotome.",
              visible: APPL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Let {BG} be the annex to {AB}.",
              visible: ANNEX,
              highlighted: ["BG"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "BG", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeExtend },
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square",
              visible: GA,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "which make the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} rational,",
              visible: GA,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "but twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} medial.",
              visible: GA,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "AB a minor", ref: "X.76" }] },
            { text: "To {CD} apply {CH}, equal to the square on {AG}, producing {CK} as breadth,",
              visible: CHS,
              highlighted: ["CD", "AG", "CK"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "K", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FKHE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and {KL}, equal to the square on {BG}, producing {KM} as breadth.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["BG", "KM"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "M", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "HKML", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "Then the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "And the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is rational, therefore {CL} is also rational.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG", "CL"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth,",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "CD", "CM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CM} is also rational and commensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CM", "CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CM rational, commensurable with CD", ref: "X.20" }] },
            { text: "Since the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "and, in these, {CE} equals the square on {AB},",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["CE", "AB"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: KLS,
              highlighted: ["FL", "AG", "BG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FL = twice AG by GB", ref: "II.7" }] },
            { text: "Bisect {FM} at the point {N},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM", "N"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "N", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] } },
            { text: "and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to either of the straight lines {CD} or {ML}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NO", "CD", "ML"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "NO", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "Then each of the rectangles {FO} and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FO", "NL", "AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "And, since twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial and equals {FL}, therefore {FL} is also medial.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG", "FL"] },
            { text: "And it is applied to the rational straight line {FE} producing {FM} as breadth,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FL", "EF", "FM"] },
            { text: "therefore {FM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM", "CD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "FM rational, incommensurable with CD", ref: "X.22" }] },
            { text: "Since the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is rational,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "while twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "therefore the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "But {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL"] },
            { text: "and {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FL"] },
            { text: "therefore {CL} is incommensurable with {FL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL", "FL"] },
            { text: "But {CL} is to {FL} as {CM} is to {MF}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CL", "FL", "CM", "FM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CL : FL = CM : MF", ref: "VI.1" }, { ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CF} is an apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CF an apotome", ref: "X.73" }] },
            { text: "I say that it is also a fourth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"] },
            { text: "Since {AG} and {GB} are incommensurable in square,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {AG} is also incommensurable with the square on {GB}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "And {CH} equals the square on {AG}, and {KL} equal to the square on {GB},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "therefore {CH} is incommensurable with {KL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "But {CH} is to {KL} as {CK} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is incommensurable in length with {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "KL", "CK", "KM"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "CH : KL = CK : KM", ref: "VI.1" }, { ref: "X.11" }] },
            { text: "Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AG", "BG"] },
            { text: "the square on {AG} equals {CH}, the square on {GB} equals {KL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {AG} by {GB} equals {NL},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NL"] },
            { text: "therefore {NL} is a mean proportional between {CH} and {KL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["NL", "CH", "KL"] },
            { text: "Therefore {CH} is to {NL} as {NL} is to {KL}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH", "NL", "KL"] },
            { text: "But {CH} is to {NL} as {CK} is to {NM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "MN"] },
            { text: "and {NL} is to {KL} as {NM} is to {KM},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["MN", "KM"] },
            { text: "therefore {CK} is to {MN} as {MN} is to {KM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "MN", "KM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.1" }, { ref: "V.11" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM", "MN"] },
            { text: "that is, to the fourth part of the square on {FM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["FM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.17" }] },
            { text: "Since {CM} and {MF} are two unequal straight lines,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {CK} by {KM}, equal to the fourth part of the square on {MF}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM", "FM"] },
            { text: "and deficient by a square figure,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM"] },
            { text: "has been applied to {CM} and divides it into incommensurable parts,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CK", "KM"] },
            { text: "therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF}",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "FM"] },
            { text: "by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "X.18" }] },
            { text: "And the whole {CM} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {CD} set out,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CM", "CD"] },
            { text: "therefore {CF} is a fourth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "fourth apotome", ref: "X.Def.III.4" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, the square on a minor straight line applied to a rational straight line",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB", "CD", "CE"] },
            { text: "produces as breadth a fourth apotome.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "X.100") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "II.7":        "/elements/books/bookII/propositions/propII7/",
        "V.11":        "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV11/",
        "VI.1":        "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI1/",
        "VI.17":       "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI17/",
        "X.11":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX11/",
        "X.18":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX18/",
        "X.20":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX20/",
        "X.22":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX22/",
        "X.73":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX73/",
        "X.76":        "/elements/books/bookX/propositions/propX76/",
        "X.Def.III.4": "/elements/books/bookX/definitions/defX.III.4/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Let {BG} be the annex to {AB}. Then {AG} and {GB} are straight lines incommensurable in square which make the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} rational, but twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} medial. [!just X.76]

To {CD} apply {CH}, equal to the square on {AG}, producing {CK} as breadth, and {KL}, equal to the square on {BG}, producing {KM} as breadth. Then the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}.

And the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is rational, therefore {CL} is also rational.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {CD} producing {CM} as breadth, therefore {CM} is also rational and commensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.20]

Since the whole {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and, in these, {CE} equals the square on {AB}, therefore the remainder {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}. [!just II.7]

Bisect {FM} at the point {N}, and draw {NO} through {N} parallel to either of the straight lines {CD} or {ML}. Then each of the rectangles {FO} and {NL} equals the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.

And, since twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial and equals {FL}, therefore {FL} is also medial.

And it is applied to the rational straight line {FE} producing {FM} as breadth, therefore {FM} is rational and incommensurable in length with {CD}. [!just X.22]

Since the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is rational, while twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is medial, therefore the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB} is incommensurable with twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}.

But {CL} equals the sum of the squares on {AG} and {GB}, and {FL} equals twice the rectangle {AG} by {GB}, therefore {CL} is incommensurable with {FL}.

But {CL} is to {FL} as {CM} is to {MF}, therefore {CM} is incommensurable in length with {MF}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

And both are rational, therefore {CM} and {MF} are rational straight lines commensurable in square only. Therefore {CF} is an apotome. [!just X.73]

I say that it is also a fourth apotome.

Since {AG} and {GB} are incommensurable in square, therefore the square on {AG} is also incommensurable with the square on {GB}. And {CH} equals the square on {AG}, and {KL} equal to the square on {GB}, therefore {CH} is incommensurable with {KL}.

But {CH} is to {KL} as {CK} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is incommensurable in length with {KM}. [!just VI.1, X.11]

Since the rectangle {AG} by {GB} is a mean proportional between the squares on {AG} and {GB} the square on {AG} equals {CH}, the square on {GB} equals {KL}, and the rectangle {AG} by {GB} equals {NL}, therefore {NL} is a mean proportional between {CH} and {KL}. Therefore {CH} is to {NL} as {NL} is to {KL}.

But {CH} is to {NL} as {CK} is to {NM}, and {NL} is to {KL} as {NM} is to {KM}, therefore {CK} is to {MN} as {MN} is to {KM}. [!just VI.1, V.11]

Therefore the rectangle {CK} by {KM} equals the square on {MN}, that is, to the fourth part of the square on {FM}. [!just VI.17]

Since {CM} and {MF} are two unequal straight lines, and the rectangle {CK} by {KM}, equal to the fourth part of the square on {MF} and deficient by a square figure, has been applied to {CM} and divides it into incommensurable parts, therefore the square on {CM} is greater than the square on {MF} by the square on a straight line incommensurable with {CM}. [!just X.18]

And the whole {CM} is commensurable in length with the rational straight line {CD} set out, therefore {CF} is a fourth apotome. [!just X.Def.III.4]

Therefore, *the square on a minor straight line applied to a rational straight line produces as breadth a fourth apotome.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
